  "sensitivity": {
    "$comment": "R10 topics. Each term is matched as a whole word or phrase (word boundaries are added). A post matching a topic is marked with it, and the mark stays on that post. A story carries a hint (sensitivity.hint) when its lead or context post matches, when at least minShare of its member posts match, or when at least minPosts of its posts match one topic; the hint never takes the rest of the story with it. Coarse on purpose: a hint for the researcher and the auditor, not a ruling. combinations: a post matching at least one term from every list in 'all' gets that topic. consentTopics are matters of consent, not subject (R11): outside a post about the show they are a general remark, not an ask to the show, so a post matching one is not marked sensitive or consent and its story stays in; it carries a repostNotes entry with the words matched, and its author's other posts in the story carry a note too, for the reviewer's repost test (R6). In a post about the show, a match is an ask to the show (see showOptOutPatterns). Every other topic marks only the post it is in (trial 002, findings 7 and 37).",
    "minShare": 0.2,
    "minPosts": 3,
